\\\"→1 (MacBook Pro 14\\\", description-only match); \\\"FLAGSHIP\\\"→1 (Samsung Galaxy S24 Ultra, tag-only match). All uppercase queries matched lowercase source data; count label matched grid size each time\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-4\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Tag-filter choice list is a static seeded set — newly assigned tags never become filter options, and removed tags remain as dead options\", \"actual\": \"After adding tag \\\"qatag-existing\\\" to the existing product Theragun Pro (and renaming \\\"massage\\\"→\\\"massage-gun\\\"), the tag filter list still contained exactly the original 35 seeded tags. \\\"qatag-existing\\\" and \\\"massage-gun\\\" were absent, so the new tag cannot be selected as a filter at all. Tags from the newly created product (\\\"qatag-alpha\\\", \\\"qatag-beta\\\") were likewise absent. Conversely the now-unused tags \\\"massage\\\", \\\"muscle\\\" and \\\"therapy\\\" are still offered; selecting \\\"muscle\\\" yields \\\"0 products found\\\". Keyword search does pick up the new tags, but the tag filter does not.\", \"evidence\": \"filters.tags list length 35, hasQatagExisting=false, hasMassageGun=false, stillHasMuscle=true; selecting \\\"muscle\\\" → \\\"0 products found\\\"\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-5\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Created \\\"QA Grip Trainer X1\\\" with new comma-separated tags \\\"qatag-alpha, qatag-beta\\\"; both render as separate tag chips on the detail page, and searching \\\"QATAG-BETA\\\" returns exactly that product (\\\"1 product found\\\")\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Theragun Pro tags edited from \\\"recovery, massage, muscle, therapy\\\" to \\\"recovery, massage-gun, qatag-existing\\\" (added qatag-existing, renamed massage→massage-gun, removed muscle+therapy). Detail page shows exactly the 3 new chips, and searching \\\"qatag-existing\\\" returns exactly Theragun Pro (\\\"1 product found\\\")\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Admin form category is a single-choice select (Tech Gadgets/Home Goods/Fitness). \\\"QA Grip Trainer X1\\\" was saved as Fitness and appears in /category/fitness (4 items) and under the Fitness badge on grid/detail; it does not appear in Tech or Home listings\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Tech→3 (Samsung, MacBook, Sony), Fitness→3 (Bowflex, Theragun, Peloton), Home→3 (Breville, Philips Hue, Dyson); count updated to \\\"3 products found\\\" each time\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"All 9 cards on /products show category badge, price, name, brief review, rating, image, and \\\"Buy Now\\\" external link (e.g. Sony WH-1000XM5: Tech | $399 | 4.8 | https://example.com/sony-xm5)\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-10\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Price-range filter is broken: it has no maximum handle and filters using a stale (one-step-behind) minimum value\", \"actual\": \"Sorting works correctly (newest, rating 4.9→4.4, price asc $199→$2,495, price desc $2,495→$199) and the min-rating filter is accurate (4.5+ → 8 products, all ≥4.5). But the price slider renders only ONE thumb (aria-label \\\"Minimum\\\"); no maximum thumb exists, so an upper bound cannot be set even though the UI displays a \\\"$0 – $2495\\\" range. The minimum also filters on the previous value: with min displayed as $700 the $699 Breville Barista Express was still listed (5 results); with min displayed as $800 the $749 Dyson V15 Detect was still listed (4 results). State persisted unchanged after a 2.5s wait, so it is not debounce.\", \"evidence\": \"min=\\\"$800\\\" → count \\\"4 products found\\\", prices $1,999 / $749 / $1,299 / $2,495\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Created products are not persisted — all admin changes are lost on page reload\", \"actual\": \"\\\"QA Minimal Product\\\" was created and appeared as a 10th row in the admin list. After reloading /admin the list was back to the original 9 seeded products and the new product was gone. localStorage, sessionStorage and document.cookie are all empty, and there is no backend API (/api/products returns the SPA HTML shell), so product data exists only in memory for the lifetime of the page.\", \"evidence\": \"Post-reload admin list = 9 seeded products only; Object.keys(localStorage)=[], sessionStorage=[], cookie=\\\"\\\"\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"All 9 seeded products carry exactly one category badge among Tech/Home/Fitness; category select offers only these three plus \\\"All Categories\\\"\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Displayed results violate the active price criterion\", \"actual\": \"With the price minimum showing $800, the result grid still included Dyson V15 Detect at $749; with the minimum at $700 it still included Breville Barista Express at $699. Each product shown is below the active minimum price, so results do not satisfy all active criteria. Category, search and rating criteria were individually respected.\", \"evidence\": \"filters.price.min=\\\"$800\\\" but products.grid contains $749\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Publish validation only enforces name, description, price and rating bounds — image, full review, valid retailer URL and specifications are not required\", \"actual\": \"Only Name and Short Description are marked required. \\\"QA Minimal Product\\\" was published successfully with an empty image URL, empty full review, empty affiliate link and zero specifications (listed as Tech | $0 | 4.5). A second product \\\"QA Bounds Probe\\\" was published with affiliate link literally \\\"not-a-valid-url\\\", again with no image, review or specs. Price/rating bounds are enforced (price -50 with rating 9 was rejected), but rejection shows no error message at all — the form silently does nothing.\", \"evidence\": \"Created row \\\"Tech | QA Bounds Probe | $10 | 4.0\\\" with affiliate-link=\\\"not-a-valid-url\\\", 0 specs, empty review/image\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-22\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"/product/does-not-exist-123 → \\\"Product Not Found — The product you're looking for doesn't exist or has been removed.\\\" with a Browse All Products action and no product.name/product.buy nodes. /category/bogus-category → \\\"Category Not Found — The category you're looking for doesn't exist.\\\" with an empty grid. Neither leaked unrelated product data\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Typing in search, changing category select, changing sort select, and moving the price slider each re-rendered the grid, order and \\\"N products found\\\" label immediately with no page reload (URL stayed /products, no navigation event)\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicking the Sony WH-1000XM5 name in the grid navigated to /product/sony-wh-1000xm5 showing that product; each card's image wrapper and name anchor both point to the same /product/{slug} href\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicking product.buy on Sony WH-1000XM5 opened a new tab at https://example.com/sony-xm5 (target=_blank, rel=noopener noreferrer). All 9 grid Buy Now links carry distinct product-specific external URLs (e.g. /macbook-pro, /dyson-v15, /peloton)\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-21\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Category select on /category/* pages is inert — choosing a different category changes nothing\", \"actual\": \"On /category/tech the category dropdown opens and lists All Categories/Tech Gadgets/Home Goods/Fitness (Tech marked aria-selected=true). Selecting \\\"Fitness\\\" and then \\\"Home Goods\\\" left everything unchanged: heading stayed \\\"Tech Gadgets\\\", trigger still displayed \\\"Tech Gadgets\\\", URL stayed /category/tech, and the grid still showed the same 3 tech products (Samsung, MacBook, Sony). Verified twice with a 600ms settle wait. The same control works correctly on /products.\", \"evidence\": \"After clicking option.home: {url:\\\"/category/tech\\\", categoryName:\\\"Tech Gadgets\\\", selectValue:\\\"Tech Gadgets\\\", items:[Samsung, MacBook, Sony]}\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"All 9 seeded detail pages show name, category badge, rating, price, brief description, full review, 4 tags, 5 key specifications, image, and Buy Now retailer link (e.g. Peloton Bike+: Fitness, 4.6, $2,495, 4 tags, 5 specs, https://example.com/peloton)\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Categories and tags are topically relevant and identical between grid and detail: Sony=Tech[headphones,wireless,noise-cancelling,premium]; MacBook=Tech[laptop,apple,professional,portable]; Samsung=Tech[smartphone,android,camera,flagship]; Dyson=Home[vacuum,cordless,smart-home,cleaning]; Hue=Home[lighting,smart-home,ambiance,automation]; Breville=Home[coffee,espresso,kitchen,appliance]; Peloton=Fitness[cardio,cycling,smart-equipment,subscription]; Theragun=Fitness[recovery,massage,muscle,therapy]; Bowflex=Fitness[weights,dumbbells,strength,home-gym]\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Sony WH-1000XM5 identical across homepage featured ($399), /products grid (Tech|$399|4.8|same brief), /category/tech grid (Tech|$399|4.8|same brief) and detail (Tech, $399, 4.8, same brief). Detail review renders in full (446 chars, line-clamp:none, scrollHeight==clientHeight) with all 5 specs; same held