    "type": "assistant_message",
    "content": "All 22 checklist items have been tested and recorded — **16 PASS, 6 FAIL**.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe core browsing, search, and detail experience is solid. The failures cluster around filtering edge cases, the featured system, validation, and persistence.\n\n**Failures found:**\n\n1. **FT-19 — No persistence (most severe).** Product data lives only in memory. `localStorage`, `sessionStorage`, and cookies are all empty and there's no backend (`/api/products` returns the SPA shell). Every product created or edited is silently lost on reload, which undermines the whole \"curate your own lists\" premise.\n\n2. **FT-10 / CS-12 — Price-range filter broken two ways.** The slider renders only one thumb (`aria-label=\"Minimum\"`) despite displaying a \"$0 – $2495\" range, so no upper bound can be set. The minimum also filters on the *previous* value — at min `$800` a `$749` product was still listed. Not a debounce; state was stable after 2.5s.\n\n3. **FT-2 — Featured system.** Toggling featured does work, but the homepage section is hard-capped at 3 (a newly featured 4th item only appeared after I unfeatured Sony). The \"View all\" link goes to `/products?featured=true`, which ignores the parameter entirely and renders all 11 products, so the complete featured set is never browsable.\n\n4. **FT-4 — Tag filter list is static.** It's a hardcoded set of 35 seeded tags. New tags never become filter options, while removed tags linger as dead options — selecting `muscle` after I removed it returns \"0 products found\". Notably, keyword search *does* index new tags correctly, so the bug is isolated to the filter list.\n\n5. **CS-20 — Weak publish validation.** Only Name and Description are required. I published a product with no image, no review, no retailer link, and zero specs; another saved with the affiliate link literally `not-a-valid-url`. Price/rating bounds *are* enforced, but rejection produces no error message at all — the form just silently does nothing.\n\n6. **IX-21 — Category select inert on category pages.** On `/category/tech`, choosing a different category leaves the heading, trigger label, URL, and grid unchanged. The identical control works fine on `/products`.\n\n**Two testing notes:** Since state is memory-only, I switched to SPA link clicks instead of URL navigation after discovering the persistence bug, so later create/edit tests wouldn't wipe their own fixtures. Also, product cards expose their semantic hint on the name anchor rather than the card container, so I read category/rating/image/buy fields from the parent card DOM to verify FT-9."
  }
}
